## Network Troubleshooting

During configuration, internet connectivity was lost.

### Root Cause

The VM had been manually assigned a static IP on an outdated VMware NAT subnet.

Originally configured:

```
192.168.237.x
```

Current VMware NAT network:

```
192.168.184.x
```

The VM could no longer communicate with the default gateway.

### Resolution

Temporarily switched the network adapter back to DHCP to discover the current VMware NAT configuration.

Obtained:

- IP Address
- Gateway
- DNS Server

Reconfigured the VM with a new static IP using the updated subnet.

Verified:

- Gateway connectivity
- Internet connectivity
- DNS resolution

